# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what a release build
# of the binary reads. New files (build artefacts, test data, editor
# droppings) stay out of the build context by default.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
# Profiles (release: LTO, strip) live here, not in Cargo.toml.
!.cargo/config.toml
!crates/
!one-research/

# Never needed by a release build, and target/ can be many GB.
**/target/
one-research/tests/
# rust-toolchain.toml is deliberately not included: the builder image is
# already pinned to the same Rust version (CI checks they match), and the
# file would make rustup download clippy/rustfmt inside the build.
